{"book":7,"chapter":5,"context":{"chapter":5,"title":"The Song of Deborah","summary":"Deborah and Barak sing of God's victory: the earth shook, the stars fought from heaven, and the river Kishon swept the enemy away. The song praises the tribes who came, rebukes those who stayed home, blesses Jael, and ends with Sisera's mother waiting in vain.","background":"Many scholars regard this song as among the oldest poetry in the Bible. It suggests a storm: the clouds poured water and the Kishon flooded (vv. 4, 21), which would have bogged down chariots. Ephraim, Benjamin, Machir, Zebulun, Issachar and Naphtali are praised; Reuben, Gilead, Dan and Asher are rebuked.","customs":[{"term":"White asses","verses":"5:10","note":"Light-colored donkeys were prized animals ridden by the wealthy and by leaders."}],"watchFor":["The roll call of tribes who came and who stayed away (vv. 14–18).","Jael's tent (vv. 24–27) set against Sisera's mother at her window (vv. 28–30).","'Let them that love him be as the sun' (v. 31)."],"connections":["Exodus 15:1-21","Deuteronomy 33:2","Psalms 68:7-8","Judges 4:15-16"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַתָּשַׁר","vatashar","H7891","Hc/Vqw3fs","and she sang"],["דְּבוֹרָה","devorah","H1683","HNpf","Deborah"],["וּבָרָק","uvarak","H1301","HC/Npm","and Barak"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אֲבִינֹעַם","'avino'am","H42","HNpm","Abinoam"],["בַּיּוֹם","baiyom","H3117","HRd/Ncmsa","on the day"],["הַהוּא","hahu'","H1931","HTd/Pp3ms","<the> that"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[2015001,2015001,6],[19018001,19018001,3],[23012001,23012006,3],[66015003,66015004,3],[66019001,66019003,3]],"xn":5},"2":{"w":[["בִּפְרֹעַ","bifroa'","H6544","HR/Vqcc","when acted as leaders"],["פְּרָעוֹת","pera'ot","H6546","HNcfpa","heads"],["בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל","beyisra'el","H3478","HR/Npl","in Israel"],["בְּהִתְנַדֵּב","behitnadev","H5068","HR/Vtcc","when volunteers"],["עָם","'am","H5971","HNcmsa","a people"],["בָּרֲכוּ","barakhu","H1288","HVpv2mp","b